# CryptoAI server contour. Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in; compose reads it automatically.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose up -d --build
#
# Only the one REQUIRED value has no default - compose refuses to start without it. Everything
# else is commented out and annotated with the default the code actually uses, so a .env with just
# that one line still produces a working server.
#
# Uncomment to change a value. Leaving a line commented means the variable is absent in the
# container and the code's own default applies; setting it to an EMPTY value is not the same thing
# and for some of these (LICENSE_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM, the AI_*_MODEL names) an empty value is a fault.

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Guards /api/keys and /api/admin/*. Those endpoints fail CLOSED when this is unset, so leaving it
# blank does not expose the admin surface - it disables it.
ADMIN_TOKEN=

# CRYPTOAI_KEK_B64 is deliberately NOT here. It is the custodial master key that unwraps every
# user's exchange and wallet secrets, and nothing in this contour needs it: trading and bots run on
# the user's own machine, and the api runs with CRYPTOAI_ROLE=edge which refuses to register the
# cipher at all. It belongs only on a separate node with no public IP, if server-side execution is
# ever reinstated. See the comment at the bottom of docker-compose.yml.

# ── Edge / TLS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hostname Caddy serves on. Set it and a certificate is obtained and renewed automatically.
# Leave it empty and the edge falls back to plain HTTP on :80 - acceptable on a laptop, not on a
# public host, because the terminal sends its licence token in a header on every request.
# CRYPTOAI_DOMAIN=api.example.com

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Change this before the FIRST boot. Postgres reads it only when the data directory is created, so
# editing it later leaves the old password in place and the api unable to connect.
DB_PASSWORD=postgres

# ── Server-side secret storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not the custodial KEK. Encrypts the server's OWN operational secrets at rest - telegram bot
# tokens, provider API keys in provider_keys. Must be identical on api and worker or the rows one
# writes read back as "not configured" in the other. Unset means those columns are stored in clear.
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
# CRYPTOAI_DATA_KEY_B64=

# ── Monitoring ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Minutes a collector may go quiet before GET /api/admin/collectors (X-Admin header) reports
# degraded. That endpoint is the thing to point an uptime monitor at; /health only proves the
# process and the database are up.
# COLLECTOR_STALE_MINUTES=120

# ── Backups ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off until the first two are set, and the backup container says so on every start rather than
# pretending to work. Until then the pgdata volume is the ONLY copy of the licence database - the
# record of money already taken from customers.
#
# restic encrypts client-side, so the bucket alone cannot read the dump. That also means
# RESTIC_PASSWORD is the whole security of the backup: keep a copy somewhere that is not this
# server, because losing it makes every snapshot permanently unreadable.
# Give the backup its own S3 key rather than reusing an app key - ideally one that can write but
# not delete, so a compromised host cannot erase the history it just uploaded.
# RESTIC_REPOSITORY=s3:https://s3.timeweb.cloud/your-bucket/cryptoai
# RESTIC_PASSWORD=
# S3_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3_SECRET_KEY=
# BACKUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=21600
# BACKUP_KEEP_DAILY=7
# BACKUP_KEEP_WEEKLY=4
# BACKUP_KEEP_MONTHLY=6

# ── Licensing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RSA public key verifying client licence tokens. Falls back to the key embedded in the app - which
# is the public half of the key the LicenseBot actually signs with, so on this deployment the
# fallback is correct and this stays unset. Set it only if the key pair is ever rotated, and set it
# in the same change that gives the bot the new private key, or every issued licence stops
# validating. An EMPTY value here is not "use the fallback": it is a key that fails to parse.
# LICENSE_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM=
# Requests per minute per licence (per IP when unauthenticated).
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=120

# ── Licence bot (sells licences over Telegram) ───────────────────────────────
# Runs in the same contour, publishes no port, needs no inbound firewall rule: Telegram is reached
# by long polling and Crypto Pay by outbound HTTPS. There is no webhook to miss, so a restart or an
# outage of this box cannot lose a payment - the bot resumes from the last update id.
#
# The signing key is NOT set here. It is mounted from ./.license-signing/private.pem, read-only,
# and must be on the server before the first start - `docker compose up` with that directory
# missing leaves the bot exiting with "License private key missing" on a loop. chmod 600.
#
# BOT_TOKEN=            # from @BotFather. Without it the bot exits immediately.
# BOT_ADMIN_IDS=        # comma-separated telegram user ids that may run /stats /recent /issue
# CRYPTOPAY_TOKEN=      # @CryptoBot -> Crypto Pay -> Create App. WITHOUT IT THE BOT CANNOT SELL:
#                       # crypto is the only payment channel now that Telegram Stars are gone.
# CRYPTOPAY_ASSETS=USDT,TON
# CRYPTOPAY_API_BASE=https://pay.crypt.bot/api/     # testnet: https://testnet-pay.crypt.bot/api/
# CRYPTO_FIAT=USD       # currency the invoice is raised in. Matches the price list, which is in
#                       # dollars because the AI cost behind every tier is billed in dollars.
# USD_RUB_RATE=80       # only for showing a rouble figure next to the dollar price
# BOT_PROVIDER_TOKEN=   # fiat payment provider, for card payments. Empty = crypto only, and with it
#                       # empty there is no auto-renewal on any channel - see docs/roadmap.

# ── AI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-held vendor keys. WITHOUT ONE every AI panel in every client correctly reports
# "AI is not set up on the server yet" - the product runs, but half of it is empty.
# These can also be set from the admin console into provider_keys, which takes effect on the next
# collector run with no redeploy.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
#
# Spend controls on the AI proxy. The request body used to be forwarded verbatim, which let a client
# choose the model, the output length and the context size while the server paid for all three.
# The allowlist MUST contain every model shipped clients actually send or this gate becomes an
# outage - current clients send claude-sonnet-4-6 and gpt-4o.
# AI_ALLOWED_ANTHROPIC_MODELS=claude-sonnet-4-6,claude-haiku-4-5-20251001,claude-sonnet-5
# AI_ALLOWED_OPENAI_MODELS=gpt-4o-mini,gpt-4o
# Clamping is silent, so keep this above the largest legitimate request (AiSignalDeskProvider: 2000).
# AI_MAX_TOKENS_CAP=2048
# AI_MAX_REQUEST_BYTES=131072
# Must clear a full agent transcript: the runners append two messages per iteration, up to 24.
# AI_MAX_MESSAGES=64
# Per-licence daily token budget, charged from the vendor's own reported usage.
# NOT ENFORCED right now: the test period ships with ai.budget.enforced = false, so this number and
# the per-tier ones are read but never applied. Spend is still counted and written to ai_usage -
# that is what the future price list gets calculated from. Turn the limit back on from /admin
# ("Суточные квоты"), not from here.
# AI_DAILY_TOKENS_PER_LICENSE=200000
#
# Models for the server's own jobs. All four default to claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 in code; set
# these only to override. Do NOT put a retired model id here - the vendor answers 404 and the job
# goes silent rather than failing loudly. claude-3-5-haiku-20241022 was the old default and was
# retired on 2026-02-19.
# AI_ASK_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# AI_SCORE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# AI_DIGEST_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# AI_ANOMALY_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# AI_PRETRADE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
#
# Cost bounds for the background AI jobs.
# AI_SCORE_BATCH=5
# AI_SCORE_MAX_AGE_HOURS=24
# AI_ANOMALY_BATCH=
# AI_ANOMALY_COOLDOWN_HOURS=
# AI_ANOMALY_MIN_MOVE_PCT=
# AI_REVIEW_BATCH=
# AI_REVIEW_DAYS=

# ── Candle collection ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tokens claimed per tick, and how often a tick runs. Mind the ceiling this implies:
# POLL_BATCH / POLL_TICK_SECONDS * 60 requests per minute at full cadence. GeckoTerminal's free
# tier is roughly 30/min, so past a few dozen hot tokens you need provider keys or a slower
# cadence - otherwise the free source starts answering 429 and candles stop.
# POLL_BATCH=50
# POLL_TICK_SECONDS=5
# POLL_CANDLE_LIMIT=60
# Tokens missing a pool address, resolved per run via DexScreener (free, no key).
# POOL_RESOLVE_BATCH=20
#
# Demand-driven backoff: a token read recently keeps full cadence, one nobody has opened in an hour
# drops back. Tokens with an active price alert are exempt, and a just-added token counts as hot.
# POLL_HOT_WINDOW_S=300
# POLL_WARM_WINDOW_S=3600
# POLL_WARM_INTERVAL_S=300
# POLL_COLD_INTERVAL_S=900

# ── Shared-response cache ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Seconds. Each is matched to how often the collector behind that endpoint actually writes:
# caching longer serves stale data, caching shorter just burns database reads.
# CACHE_TTL_CANDLES=20
# CACHE_TTL_TOKEN=20
# CACHE_TTL_NEWS=60
# CACHE_TTL_SENTIMENT=120
# CACHE_TTL_GAS=30
# CACHE_TTL_ONCHAIN=300
# CACHE_TTL_WHALES=60
# CACHE_TTL_LIQUIDATIONS=60
# CACHE_TTL_DIGESTS=120
# Largest watchlist served in one composite request.
# WATCHLIST_MAX_TOKENS=200

# ── Custodial (dormant: trading and bots run on the user's machine) ───────────
# WITHDRAWAL_DELAY_MINUTES=30
# MANUAL_MAX_NOTIONAL_USD=5000

# ── Collector watchdog ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reports a failing or silent collector to Telegram: once when it breaks, once when it recovers,
# one reminder a day while it stays broken. Reuse the licence bot's token or make a second bot;
# ALERT_CHAT_ID is your own Telegram id (ask @userinfobot). Unset - the watchdog logs and stays quiet.
# ALERT_BOT_TOKEN=
# ALERT_CHAT_ID=
